## Important Warning

This package is significantly more invasive than a simple script hotfix.

The author recommends completely replacing SLHH.

Because NEFARAM-Rhiven currently contains an established SLHH / SLHH Expansion / SexLab Approach environment, replacing the entire system may affect:

- scripts;
- quests;
- dialogue;
- MCM settings;
- scene conditions;
- existing save data;
- integrations with other Baka-related mods.

The package must therefore not be installed directly into the stable profile without prior analysis.

---

## Recommended Investigation Procedure

If problems with SLHH or SexLab Approach are reproduced on NEFARAM-Rhiven:

1. Confirm the exact symptoms.
2. Record installed versions of:
   - SLHH;
   - SLHH Expansion;
   - SexLab Approach.
3. Archive the current versions.
4. Inspect the community package contents.
5. Compare:
   - ESP/ESM records;
   - Papyrus scripts;
   - MCM files;
   - interface files;
   - configuration files.
6. Determine whether the package replaces or modifies:
   - quests;
   - scenes;
   - dialogue;
   - aliases;
   - scripts;
   - properties.
7. Compare modified `.pex` files using Champollion when possible.
8. Test only on a copied profile or dedicated test save.
9. Verify whether the addon patch correctly overwrites SLHH Expansion.
10. Confirm that all existing NEFARAM integrations still function.
11. Check Papyrus logs.
12. Test repeated approaches and scene cleanup.
13. Test save/reload behaviour.
14. Only integrate the package after successful validation.

---

## Symptoms That May Justify Testing This Package

Consider investigating this package if NEFARAM-Rhiven exhibits:

- approaches that fail to trigger;
- scenes that fail to start;
- dialogue branches that skip expected events;
- incorrect approach-type behaviour;
- aura problems;
- house-visit failures;
- deployed actors remaining in cities;
- scenes that cannot be stopped;
- missing post-scene dialogue;
- SLHH or SLAPP quests becoming stuck.

